# Normalize line endings to LF for all text files.
#
# Rationale: many unit tests read source files and assert on exact line
# structure (e.g. `source.split("\n")` compared against fixed arrays). With no
# eol policy, a Windows checkout under core.autocrlf=true materializes CRLF,
# leaving a stray "\r" on every line and failing those eol-sensitive tests --
# and inflating `git status`/diffs with phantom eol-only changes. Pinning the
# working tree to LF makes source scans, diffs, and tests deterministic across
# Windows, Linux, and CI, independent of each machine's local git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shell scripts must stay CRLF if any are added later.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
